  "family": "classical",
  "lineage": "Korean sanjo (\"scattered melody\") solo virtuoso instrumental tradition emerging in late-nineteenth-century southwestern Korea (Jeolla provinces) and crystallizing into the canonical concert form through Kim Chang-jo (1865-1919) for the gayageum zither and subsequent adaptations for geomungo, daegeum, ajaeng, and haegeum. Performance is a continuous suite of progressively accelerating sections (jinyangjo, jungmori, jungjungmori, jajinmori, hwimori, danmori), with janggu hourglass-drum accompaniment marking the rhythmic-cycle changgu. The sanjo grew from sinawi shaman-ensemble heterophony into a self-standing virtuoso art-music form parallel to but distinct from pansori vocal narrative.",
